.TH banner 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
banner \- print large letters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B banner
.I "string ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B banner
prints each argument in large letters across the screen, one banner per
argument with a blank line between them.
.PP
Each letter is drawn out of copies of itself rather than out of a fixed
character, so
.B banner
.B HELLO
is drawn in H, E, L and O.  Capitals are seven rows high, lower case
six, and case is kept as you typed it.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
Letters, digits and the common punctuation are all there.  Nothing wraps
\- a long argument simply runs off the right of an 80 column screen, so
break it into several arguments instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR echo (1),
.BR write (1)
